<Wiki
  title="Scope"
  description="What the PUV binary actually does: commands, files, and the Composer behavior it does not copy."
>
  <p class="kicker">Wiki</p>
  <h1>Scope</h1>
  <p>
    PUV is one Rust binary. The crates inside it are not separate tools you install. Composer’s
    package names, version constraints, and the Composer v2 metadata API are the interface to
    Packagist. The resolver, cache, environment, and PHP builds are PUV’s.
  </p>

  <h2>Commands</h2>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Command</th><th>Does</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>puv init</td><td>Writes puv.toml, src/main.php, .gitignore</td></tr>
      <tr><td>puv add &lt;pkg&gt;</td><td>Manifest, resolve, lock, install</td></tr>
      <tr><td>puv add --dev &lt;pkg&gt;</td><td>Same, into dev-dependencies</td></tr>
      <tr><td>puv install &lt;pkg&gt;</td><td>Alias of add</td></tr>
      <tr><td>puv install</td><td>Alias of sync</td></tr>
      <tr><td>puv remove &lt;pkg&gt;</td><td>Drop, relock, sync</td></tr>
      <tr><td>puv lock</td><td>Resolve and write puv.lock</td></tr>
      <tr><td>puv lock --upgrade</td><td>Ignore locked versions</td></tr>
      <tr><td>puv lock &lt;pkg&gt;</td><td>Upgrade that one package inside its constraint</td></tr>
      <tr><td>puv sync</td><td>Install the lock. No resolve</td></tr>
      <tr><td>puv use &lt;version&gt;</td><td>Set the project PHP line and install it</td></tr>
      <tr><td>puv use --global</td><td>Set the user pin</td></tr>
      <tr><td>puv php list</td><td>Index plus what is installed</td></tr>
      <tr><td>puv php install / remove</td><td>Manage one runtime</td></tr>
      <tr><td>puv run …</td><td>File, script, project tool, then .puv/bin</td></tr>
      <tr><td>puv &lt;file.php&gt;</td><td>Same as puv run</td></tr>
      <tr><td>puv -c</td><td>Inline PHP on the project runtime</td></tr>
      <tr><td>puv load &lt;pkg&gt;</td><td>Project-local tool, own environment</td></tr>
      <tr><td>puv tool install</td><td>Global tool, own environment, shim in ~/.local/bin</td></tr>
      <tr><td>puv tool list / upgrade / uninstall</td><td>Those shims and environments</td></tr>
      <tr><td>puv check</td><td>Syntax and project consistency</td></tr>
      <tr><td>puv build</td><td>Sync, then the build script, with PUV_BUILD=1</td></tr>
      <tr><td>puv run build</td><td>The script only</td></tr>
      <tr><td>puv package</td><td>PHAR by default, or zip, or tar</td></tr>
      <tr><td>puv contain</td><td>composer.lock into puv.lock, originals kept</td></tr>
      <tr><td>puv contain --clean</td><td>Then delete composer.json, composer.lock, vendor/</td></tr>
      <tr><td>puv prune --global</td><td>Drop cache entries nothing references</td></tr>
      <tr><td>puv prune --global --all</td><td>Empty the cache. Installed tools and runtimes stay</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Files</h2>
  <p>
    <code>puv.toml</code> is the manifest. <code>puv.lock</code> is the dependency graph you
    commit. <code>.puv/lockb</code> is a cache of the parsed lock for faster <code>run</code> and
    <code>sync</code>. It is not a second source of truth: if the bytes of <code>puv.lock</code>
    change, the cache is discarded.
  </p>
  <pre class="block">~/.cache/puv/          packages, runtimes, metadata, indexes
~/.local/share/puv/    installed PHP builds, global tools, the pin
~/.local/bin/          shims from puv tool install

.puv/
├── env.json
├── autoload.php
├── bin/
├── deps/              symlinks into the content-addressed cache
└── tools/&lt;name&gt;/      one environment per loaded tool</pre>
  <p>
    <code>PUV_CACHE_DIR</code>, <code>PUV_DATA_DIR</code>, and <code>PUV_BIN_DIR</code> move
    those three roots.
  </p>

  <h2>Resolution</h2>
  <p>
    Metadata is Composer v2: <code>https://repo.packagist.org/p2/vendor/package.json</code>. The
    minified version list is expanded in Rust. The solver is PubGrub. It picks the highest
    stable version, and a locked version first when one still fits. <code>php</code>,
    <code>ext-*</code>, <code>lib-*</code>, <code>composer-plugin-api</code>, and
    <code>composer-runtime-api</code> are virtual packages. <code>provide</code>,
    <code>replace</code>, and <code>conflict</code> are part of the solve.
  </p>
  <p>
    Minimum stability in this version is stable. <code>dev-main</code> and inline aliases are
    not. A required extension missing from the runtime’s fixed set fails the lock instead of
    being downloaded later.
  </p>

  <h2>What this is not</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>PUV does not shell out to <code>composer</code>, and it does not link Composer as a library.</li>
    <li>It does not run scripts from a downloaded <code>composer.json</code>.</li>
    <li>It does not load Composer plugins, and <code>contain</code> will say so when it skips them.</li>
    <li>It does not treat <code>vendor/</code> as the project layout. Autoload is injected.</li>
    <li>It does not compile PHP from php-src. Runtimes are prebuilt glibc CLI builds.</li>
    <li>It does not embed the PHP runtime inside a PHAR.</li>
    <li>Published install artifacts are Linux only. macOS and Windows are not in the release set the installer understands.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    A normal library or CLI project with a lockfile is the migration target.
    <code>puv contain</code> copies string scripts, skips PHP callables and
    <code>@composer</code> lines, and leaves the Composer files in place.
  </p>
</Wiki>
